      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d like to see us never use str % operator without explicitly passing a tuple, since if a tuple ever sneaks in by mistake, we\u0027ll end up with a misleading error or a misleading formatted string.\n\nIn other words, instead of:\n  \u0027foo: %r\u0027 % one_var\nAlways do:\n  \u0027foo: %r\u0027 % (one_var,)\n\nAlternatively, if singleton tuples are too ugly, we could move to the newer string formatting syntax:\n  \u0027foo: {!r}\u0027.format(one_var)\n\nNo action needed in this CL, this CL is a strict improvement even without that additional cleanup.",
      "revId": "9dbfd3d08db601764ded39e1cf143d78844e31a4",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
